Ladybird accepts a navigation download from the process preparing
its response or populating its destination document. The navigation
ends without replacing the active document, and the downloader
adopts the response body from the original request.

Blink’s NavigationRequest::OnWillProcessResponseChecksComplete()
hands download responses to DownloadManagerImpl::InterceptNavigation
and cancels navigation. WebKit’s WebPageProxy::receivedPolicyDecision
response overload creates a DownloadProxy for PolicyAction::Download
and preserves the redirect chain. Gecko’s nsDocumentOpenInfo::
DispatchContent() retargets attachment responses to the external
helper service. Ladybird matches their behavior: The response becomes
a download without committing a replacement document.
